<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sevastopol</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Sebastopol</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sevastopol is a port city in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crimea">Crimea</a>, founded by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a> in 1783 as the base of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea-fleet">Black Sea Fleet</a>, near the ruins of Greek Chersonesus. It withstood long sieges in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crimean-war">Crimean War</a> (1854–1855) and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a> (1941–1942). Annexed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> in 2014 with the rest of Crimea, it is internationally recognised as part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sevastopol.jpg" alt="Sevastopol" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: GIC198 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:1356_%D0%9F%D0%B0%D0%BC%D1%8F%D1%82%D0%BD%D0%B8%D0%BA_%D0%B7%D0%B0%D1%82%D0%BE%D0%BF%D0%BB%D0%B5%D0%BD%D0%BD%D1%8B%D0%BC_%D0%BA%D0%BE%D1%80%D0%B0%D0%B1%D0%BB%D1%8F%D0%BC.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
